/-!
# The Chern classes of the exterior powers of a finite locally free module

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project, let `X` be locally of
finite type over `S` and let `ℰ` be a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module of rank `r ≥ 1`.
[Stacks, Tag 0FEE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEE) is the identity

  `∏_{n = 0}^{r} c(⋀ⁿ ℰ)^{(-1)ⁿ} = 1 - (r-1)! c_r(ℰ) + …`

for the total Chern classes in the ring `Stacks.Chow.TotalChowClass C sX = ∏_{p ≥ 0} A^p(X)` of
total Chow cohomology classes, where `c_i(ℰ) = TotalChowClass.homComponent i (totalChern C sX ℰ r)`
is the bivariant Chern class of Stacks 0B7H. The source's proof ends "the first nonzero term in our
Chern class is in degree `r` and equal to the predicted value": the `+ …` asserts nothing about the
parts above degree `r`, and the lemma is the vanishing of the parts in degrees `1, …, r - 1`
together with the value of the part in degree `r`.

## The proof

The source's proof is followed.

* **The splitting principle.** By Stacks 02UL two total classes agree as soon as they agree after
  restriction along every `h : T ⟶ X` along which `h^*ℰ` has a filtration with invertible
  successive quotients (`Stacks.Chow.TotalChowClass.eq_of_res_eq_of_hasInvertibleFiltration`).
  Restriction commutes with the alternating product, the exterior powers commuting with pullback
  (Stacks 01CI).
* **The Chern roots.** On such a `T`, with `x_1, …, x_r` the first Chern classes of the
  successive quotients,

    `c(⋀ⁿ h^*ℰ) = ∏_{1 ≤ i_1 < ⋯ < i_n ≤ r} (1 + x_{i_1} + ⋯ + x_{i_n})`,

  which is the display of the source proof (`Stacks.Chow.exists_chernRoots_exteriorPower`). It
  is proved by induction along the filtration read from its bottom step `0 ⟶ ℒ ⟶ ℳ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0`,
  `ℒ` of rank one: the exterior powers sit in the short exact sequences
  `0 ⟶ ℒ ⊗ ⋀^k 𝒬 ⟶ ⋀^{k+1} ℳ ⟶ ⋀^{k+1} 𝒬 ⟶ 0`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_shortExact_exteriorPower_of_rank_one`), so the
  Whitney sum formula (Stacks 02UI) and the twist formula (Stacks 02UD) split the subsets
  `I ⊆ {1, …, r}` according to whether they contain the root `c₁(ℒ)`.
* **The computation.** The alternating product of these explicit products is computed by
  `Stacks.Chow.homPart_alternatingProd_of_roots`. Instead of the source's logarithm, the
  alternating product is regrouped over all subsets `I` into
  `(∏_{#I even} (1 + s_I)) · (∏_{#I odd} (1 + s_I))^{-1}`, `s_I = ∑_{i ∈ I} x_i`, and the
  degreewise comparison of the two halves is `AlgebraicGeometry.subsetSumEsymm_even_eq_odd`
  and `AlgebraicGeometry.subsetSumEsymm_even_sub_odd`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.chernBicommutant` — the commutative subring of `∏_p A^p(X)` of the classes
  commuting with everything that commutes with all Chern classes; it contains the inverses of
  the total Chern classes.
* `Stacks.Chow.altExteriorTotalChern` — the alternating product `∏_{n = 0}^{r} c(⋀ⁿ ℰ)^{(-1)ⁿ}`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.homPart_alternatingProd_of_roots` — the computation in terms of Chern roots.
* `Stacks.Chow.twist_coe_prod_one_add` — the twist of a product `∏ (1 + y_k)`.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_chernRoots_exteriorPower` — the Chern roots of the exterior powers of a
  module with a filtration by invertible quotients.
* `Stacks.Chow.res_altExteriorTotalChern` — restriction of the alternating product.
* `Stacks.Chow.homPart_altExteriorTotalChern` — **Stacks 0FEE.**

## Implementation notes

The ring of total classes is not known to be commutative, so the alternating product is an
ordered product of units, as for the total Chern class of a bounded complex
(`Stacks.Chow.complexChernProd`). The computation is carried out in
`Stacks.Chow.chernBicommutant`, which is commutative and, unlike the ring
`Stacks.Chow.chernRing` generated by the Chern classes, closed under the inverses the
alternating product needs.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B7H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B7H)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Finset

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

open TotalChowClass

/-! ### The bicommutant of the Chern classes -/

section Bicommutant

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- **The bicommutant of the Chern classes**: the total classes commuting with every total class
that commutes with all Chern classes `c_i(ℰ)`. It is a commutative subring of
`∏_p A^p(X)` containing the ring `Stacks.Chow.chernRing` of Chern classes, and unlike that ring
it contains the inverse of each of its elements which is a unit of `∏_p A^p(X)`, such as a total
Chern class `c(ℰ)`. -/
abbrev chernBicommutant : Subring (TotalChowClass C sX) :=
  Subring.centralizer (Subring.centralizer (chernSet C sX) : Set (TotalChowClass C sX))

/-- The bicommutant of the Chern classes is commutative, the Chern classes commuting with each
other. -/
instance : CommRing (chernBicommutant C sX) :=
  { (chernBicommutant C sX).toRing with
    mul_comm := fun a b => Subtype.ext <|
      Set.centralizer_centralizer_comm_of_comm
        (fun x hx y hy _ => chernSet_commute C sX x hx y hy) _ a.2 _ b.2 }

/-- The Chern classes lie in their bicommutant. -/
theorem chernRing_le_chernBicommutant : chernRing C sX ≤ chernBicommutant C sX :=
  Subring.closure_le.2 Set.subset_centralizer_centralizer

/-- **An element of the bicommutant which is a unit of `∏_p A^p(X)` is a unit of the
bicommutant**: its inverse commutes with everything it commutes with. -/
theorem isUnit_chernBicommutant_of_isUnit_coe {a : chernBicommutant C sX}
    (ha : IsUnit (a : TotalChowClass C sX)) : IsUnit a := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := ha
  have hmem : (↑v⁻¹ : TotalChowClass C sX) ∈ chernBicommutant C sX := by
    rw [Subring.mem_centralizer_iff]
    intro y hy
    have hc : Commute (v : TotalChowClass C sX) y := by
      have := (Subring.mem_centralizer_iff.1 a.2) y hy
      rw [hv]
      exact this.symm
    exact (hc.units_inv_left).eq.symm
  refine isUnit_iff_exists_inv.2 ⟨⟨_, hmem⟩, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  change (a : TotalChowClass C sX) * ↑v⁻¹ = 1
  rw [← hv, Units.mul_inv]

end Bicommutant

/-! ### Homogeneous parts of products of classes of degree one -/

section Homogeneous

variable {C : ChowSituation.{u}} {X : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ C.S} [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- A product of `#p` elements of degree one of the bicommutant is homogeneous of degree `#p`. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_coe_prod {κ : Type*} (p : Finset κ) (y : κ → chernBicommutant C sX)
    (hy : ∀ k, (y k : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1) :
    ((∏ k ∈ p, y k : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous #p := by
  classical
  induction p using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty => exact isHomogeneous_one
  | insert a s ha ih =>
    rw [Finset.prod_insert ha, Subring.coe_mul, Finset.card_insert_of_notMem ha, Nat.add_comm]
    exact (hy a).mul ih

/-- **The homogeneous parts of `∏ (1 + y_k)`** for elements `y_k` of degree one of the
bicommutant: the degree-`n` part is the `n`-th elementary symmetric function of the `y_k`. -/
theorem homPart_coe_prod_one_add {κ : Type*} (p : Finset κ) (y : κ → chernBicommutant C sX)
    (hy : ∀ k, (y k : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1) (n : ℕ) :
    TotalChowClass.homComponent n
        ((∏ k ∈ p, (1 + y k) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) =
      ((∑ T ∈ p.powersetCard n, ∏ k ∈ T, y k : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) := by
  classical
  rw [Finset.prod_one_add, AddSubmonoidClass.coe_finsetSum, map_sum,
    AddSubmonoidClass.coe_finsetSum, Finset.powersetCard_eq_filter, Finset.sum_filter]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun T _ => ?_
  split_ifs with hT
  · subst hT
    exact (isHomogeneous_coe_prod T y hy).homComponent_self
  · exact (isHomogeneous_coe_prod T y hy).homPart_of_ne (Ne.symm hT)

/-- The subset sums `∑_{i ∈ I} t_i` of elements of degree one are of degree one. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_coe_sum {κ : Type*} (I : Finset κ) (t : κ → chernBicommutant C sX)
    (ht : ∀ i, (t i : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1) :
    ((∑ i ∈ I, t i : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1 := by
  rw [AddSubmonoidClass.coe_finsetSum]
  exact IsHomogeneous.sum fun i _ => ht i

/-- The degree-`r` part of `∏_{i < r} (1 + t_i)` is `t_1 ⋯ t_r`, the top Chern class in terms of
the Chern roots. -/
theorem homPart_coe_prod_one_add_univ {r : ℕ} (t : Fin r → chernBicommutant C sX)
    (ht : ∀ i, (t i : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1) :
    TotalChowClass.homComponent r ((∏ i, (1 + t i) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) =
      ((∏ i, t i : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) := by
  rw [homPart_coe_prod_one_add _ t ht]
  have hps : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)).powersetCard r = {Finset.univ} := by
    have h := Finset.powersetCard_self (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r))
    rwa [Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin] at h
  rw [hps, Finset.sum_singleton]

end Homogeneous

/-! ### Twisting products of classes of degree one -/

section Twist

variable {C : ChowSituation.{u}} {X : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ C.S} [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- `T_{1,x}(1) = 1 + x` for `x` of degree one: the total Chern class of an invertible module
`ℒ`, as the twist of the trivial module of rank one. -/
theorem twist_one_one {x : TotalChowClass C sX} (hx : x.IsHomogeneous 1) :
    twist 1 x 1 = 1 + x := by
  refine ext_homPart fun m => ?_
  rw [homPart_twist hx, Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem m (Finset.mem_range.2 m.lt_succ_self)]
  · rw [Nat.sub_self, isHomogeneous_one.homComponent_self, one_mul,
      show (1 : ℤ) - m + m = ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ) by push_cast; ring, Ring.choose_natCast, map_add,
      natCast_zsmul]
    rcases m with _ | _ | m
    · rw [Nat.choose_zero_right, one_smul, pow_zero, isHomogeneous_one.homComponent_self,
        hx.homPart_of_ne (by omega), add_zero]
    · rw [Nat.choose_self, one_smul, pow_one, isHomogeneous_one.homPart_of_ne (by omega),
        hx.homComponent_self, zero_add]
    · rw [Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt (by omega), zero_smul,
        isHomogeneous_one.homPart_of_ne (by omega), hx.homPart_of_ne (by omega), add_zero]
  · intro j hj hjm
    have hjm' : j < m := lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.lt_succ_iff.1 (Finset.mem_range.1 hj)) hjm
    rw [isHomogeneous_one.homPart_of_ne (by omega), zero_mul, smul_zero]

/-- `T_{1,x}(y) = y` for `x` and `y` of degree one. -/
theorem twist_one_of_isHomogeneous_one {x y : TotalChowClass C sX} (hx : x.IsHomogeneous 1)
    (hy : y.IsHomogeneous 1) : twist 1 x y = y := by
  refine ext_homPart fun m => ?_
  rw [homPart_twist hx]
  rcases m with _ | m
  · rw [Finset.sum_range_one, hy.homPart_of_ne (by omega), zero_mul, smul_zero]
  · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem m (Finset.mem_range.2 (by omega))]
    · rw [show m + 1 - m = 1 by omega, hy.homComponent_self,
        show (1 : ℤ) - ((m + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + (m : ℤ) = 0 by push_cast; ring]
      rcases m with _ | m
      · rw [Ring.choose_zero_right, one_smul, pow_zero, mul_one, hy.homComponent_self]
      · rw [Ring.choose_zero_succ, zero_smul, hy.homPart_of_ne (by omega)]
    · intro j hj hjm
      have hjm' : j ≤ m + 1 := Nat.lt_succ_iff.1 (Finset.mem_range.1 hj)
      rw [hy.homPart_of_ne (by omega), zero_mul, smul_zero]

/-- **The twist of a product of `1 + y_k`**: for `x` and the `y_k` of degree one in the
bicommutant of the Chern classes, `T_{#q,x}(∏_{k ∈ q} (1 + y_k)) = ∏_{k ∈ q} (1 + x + y_k)`. In
terms of Chern roots this is the twist formula `c(ℒ ⊗ ℰ) = ∏ (1 + c₁(ℒ) + x_k)` of
Stacks 02UD. -/
theorem twist_coe_prod_one_add (x : chernBicommutant C sX)
    (hx : (x : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1) {κ : Type*} (q : Finset κ)
    (y : κ → chernBicommutant C sX) (hy : ∀ k, (y k : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1) :
    twist (#q : ℤ) (x : TotalChowClass C sX)
        ((∏ k ∈ q, (1 + y k) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) =
      ((∏ k ∈ q, (1 + (x + y k)) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) := by
  classical
  induction q using Finset.induction_on with
  | empty =>
    rw [Finset.card_empty, Nat.cast_zero, Finset.prod_empty, Finset.prod_empty, Subring.coe_one]
    exact twist_zero_one hx
  | insert a q ha ih =>
    rw [Finset.prod_insert ha, Finset.prod_insert ha, Finset.card_insert_of_notMem ha,
      Nat.cast_succ, add_comm (#q : ℤ) 1, Subring.coe_mul, Subring.coe_mul,
      twist_mul hx 1 (#q : ℤ) _ (show Commute (x : TotalChowClass C sX)
        ((∏ k ∈ q, (1 + y k) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) from
        (Commute.all x (∏ k ∈ q, (1 + y k))).map (chernBicommutant C sX).subtype), ih,
      Subring.coe_add, Subring.coe_one, map_add, twist_one_one hx,
      twist_one_of_isHomogeneous_one hx (hy a), Subring.coe_add, Subring.coe_add,
      Subring.coe_one, add_assoc]

end Twist

/-! ### Subsets of `Fin (m + 1)` -/

/-- **The subsets of size `k + 1` of `{0, …, m}`**, split according to whether they contain `0`:
for `t = (a, y_1, …, y_m)`, a product over them of a function of the subset sums of `t` is the
product over the subsets `J` of size `k` of `{1, …, m}` at `a + ∑_J y` times the product over
those of size `k + 1` at `∑_J y`. -/
theorem prod_powersetCard_succ_cons {R M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid R] [CommMonoid M] (g : R → M)
    {m : ℕ} (a : R) (y : Fin m → R) (k : ℕ) :
    ∏ I ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin (m + 1))).powersetCard (k + 1),
        g (∑ i ∈ I, (Fin.cons a y : Fin (m + 1) → R) i) =
      (∏ J ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin m)).powersetCard k, g (a + ∑ j ∈ J, y j)) *
        ∏ J ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin m)).powersetCard (k + 1), g (∑ j ∈ J, y j) := by
  classical
  have hu : (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin (m + 1))) =
      insert 0 ((Finset.univ : Finset (Fin m)).map (Fin.succAboveEmb 0)) := by
    rw [Fin.univ_succAbove m 0, Finset.cons_eq_insert]
  have h0 : (0 : Fin (m + 1)) ∉ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin m)).map (Fin.succAboveEmb 0) := by
    simp [Fin.succAboveEmb, Fin.succ_ne_zero]
  have hsum : ∀ J : Finset (Fin m),
      ∑ i ∈ J.map (Fin.succAboveEmb 0), (Fin.cons a y : Fin (m + 1) → R) i = ∑ j ∈ J, y j :=
    fun J => by
      rw [Finset.sum_map]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by simp [Fin.succAboveEmb]
  rw [hu, Finset.powersetCard_succ_insert h0, Finset.prod_union, mul_comm]
  · congr 1
    · rw [Finset.prod_image]
      · rw [Finset.powersetCard_map, Finset.prod_map]
        refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun J hJ => ?_
        simp only [Finset.mapEmbedding_apply, RelEmbedding.coe_toEmbedding]
        rw [Finset.sum_insert, hsum]
        · rfl
        · simp [Fin.succAboveEmb, Fin.succ_ne_zero]
      · intro I hI I' hI' hII'
        have hI0 : (0 : Fin (m + 1)) ∉ I := fun h => h0
          ((Finset.mem_powersetCard.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 hI)).1 h)
        have hI0' : (0 : Fin (m + 1)) ∉ I' := fun h => h0
          ((Finset.mem_powersetCard.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 hI')).1 h)
        rw [← Finset.erase_insert hI0, ← Finset.erase_insert hI0']
        exact congrArg (fun S => Finset.erase S 0) hII'
    · rw [Finset.powersetCard_map, Finset.prod_map]
      refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun J _ => ?_
      simp only [Finset.mapEmbedding_apply, RelEmbedding.coe_toEmbedding]
      rw [hsum]
  · refine Finset.disjoint_left.2 fun I h1 h2 => ?_
    obtain ⟨I', _, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 h2
    exact h0 ((Finset.mem_powersetCard.1 h1).1 (Finset.mem_insert_self 0 I'))

/-! ### The alternating product -/

section Alternating

variable {C : ChowSituation.{u}} {X : Scheme.{u}} {sX : X ⟶ C.S} [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- An ordered product over `0, …, m - 1` in a commutative monoid is the product over the
range. -/
private theorem list_prod_map_range {M : Type*} [CommMonoid M] (f : ℕ → M) (m : ℕ) :
    ((List.range m).map f).prod = ∏ n ∈ Finset.range m, f n := by
  induction m with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ m ih =>
    rw [List.range_succ, List.map_append, List.prod_append, ih, Finset.prod_range_succ]
    simp

/-- **The alternating product of the total classes predicted by Chern roots.** Let
`t_1, …, t_r` (`r ≥ 1`) be elements of degree one of the bicommutant of the Chern classes and let
`u_n` be units of `∏_p A^p(X)` with `u_n = ∏_{#I = n} (1 + ∑_{i ∈ I} t_i)` for `n ≤ r`. Then the
ordered product `∏_{n = 0}^{r} u_n^{(-1)^n}` has vanishing homogeneous parts in the degrees
`1, …, r - 1`, and its degree-`r` part is `-(r-1)! t_1 ⋯ t_r`.

This is the computation of Stacks 0FEE in terms of the Chern roots; the cancellation is
`AlgebraicGeometry.subsetSumEsymm_even_eq_odd` and `AlgebraicGeometry.subsetSumEsymm_even_sub_odd`
of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.SplittingPrinciple.AlternatingSubsetSums`. -/
theorem homPart_alternatingProd_of_roots {r : ℕ} (hr : r ≠ 0)
    (t : Fin r → chernBicommutant C sX) (ht : ∀ i, (t i : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1)
    (u : ℕ → (TotalChowClass C sX)ˣ)
    (hu : ∀ n ≤ r, (u n : TotalChowClass C sX) =
      ((∏ I ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)).powersetCard n, (1 + ∑ i ∈ I, t i) :
        chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX)) :
    (∀ n, 0 < n → n < r → TotalChowClass.homComponent n
        ((((List.range (r + 1)).map fun n => u n ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ n)).prod :
          (TotalChowClass C sX)ˣ) : TotalChowClass C sX) = 0) ∧
      TotalChowClass.homComponent r
          ((((List.range (r + 1)).map fun n => u n ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ n)).prod :
            (TotalChowClass C sX)ˣ) : TotalChowClass C sX) =
        -(Nat.factorial (r - 1) • ((∏ i, t i : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX)) := by
  classical
  -- the subset sums and the units `1 + s_I` of the bicommutant
  set s : Finset (Fin r) → chernBicommutant C sX := fun I => ∑ i ∈ I, t i
  have hsh : ∀ I, ((s I : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX).IsHomogeneous 1 := fun I =>
    isHomogeneous_coe_sum I t ht
  have hunit : ∀ I, IsUnit (1 + s I) := fun I => isUnit_chernBicommutant_of_isUnit_coe C sX
    (TotalChowClass.isUnit_of_apply_zero (by
      rw [Subring.coe_add, Subring.coe_one, TotalChowClass.add_apply, hsh I 0 (by omega),
        add_zero]))
  let w : Finset (Fin r) → (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ := fun I => (hunit I).unit
  have hw : ∀ I, ((w I : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ) : chernBicommutant C sX) = 1 + s I :=
    fun I => (hunit I).unit_spec
  -- the factors `u n`, read in the bicommutant
  have hfac : ∀ n ∈ Finset.range (r + 1), u n =
      Units.map ((chernBicommutant C sX).subtype : chernBicommutant C sX →* TotalChowClass C sX)
        (∏ I ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)).powersetCard n, w I) := fun n hn => by
    refine Units.ext ?_
    rw [hu n (Nat.lt_succ_iff.1 (Finset.mem_range.1 hn)), Units.coe_map, MonoidHom.coe_ofClass,
      Subring.coe_subtype, Units.coe_prod]
    exact congrArg Subtype.val (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun I _ => (hw I).symm)
  set P : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ := ∏ n ∈ Finset.range (r + 1),
    (∏ I ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)).powersetCard n, w I) ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ n) with hPdef
  have hlist : ((List.range (r + 1)).map fun n => u n ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ n)).prod =
      Units.map ((chernBicommutant C sX).subtype :
        chernBicommutant C sX →* TotalChowClass C sX) P := by
    rw [hPdef, ← list_prod_map_range, map_list_prod, List.map_map]
    refine congrArg List.prod (List.map_congr_left fun n hn => ?_)
    rw [Function.comp_apply, map_zpow, hfac n (Finset.mem_range.2 (List.mem_range.1 hn))]
  -- regrouping over all subsets of `Fin r`
  have hcu : #(Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)) = r := by simp
  set Qe : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ := ∏ I ∈ evenCardSubsets r, w I with hQe
  set Qo : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ := ∏ I ∈ oddCardSubsets r, w I with hQo
  have hregroup : P * Qo = Qe := by
    have h1 : P = ∏ I : Finset (Fin r), w I ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ #I) := by
      rw [hPdef]
      have h := Finset.prod_powerset (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r))
        (fun I => w I ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ #I))
      rw [hcu, Finset.powerset_univ] at h
      rw [h]
      refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun n _ => ?_
      rw [← Finset.prod_zpow]
      exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun I hI => by rw [(Finset.mem_powersetCard.1 hI).2]
    rw [h1, ← Finset.prod_filter_mul_prod_filter_not Finset.univ
        (fun I : Finset (Fin r) => Even #I),
      hQe, hQo, evenCardSubsets, oddCardSubsets, mul_assoc, ← Finset.prod_mul_distrib]
    have h2 : ∏ I ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun I : Finset (Fin r) => ¬ Even #I),
        w I ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ #I) * w I = 1 := by
      refine Finset.prod_eq_one fun I hI => ?_
      rw [Odd.neg_one_pow (Nat.not_even_iff_odd.1 (Finset.mem_filter.1 hI).2), zpow_neg_one,
        inv_mul_cancel]
    rw [h2, mul_one]
    exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun I hI => by
      rw [Even.neg_one_pow (Finset.mem_filter.1 hI).2, zpow_one]
  -- the values in `∏_p A^p(X)`
  have hval : ((((List.range (r + 1)).map fun n => u n ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ n)).prod :
      (TotalChowClass C sX)ˣ) : TotalChowClass C sX) =
      (((P : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) := by
    rw [hlist]
    rfl
  rw [hval]
  have hcoeQ : ∀ p : Finset (Finset (Fin r)), ((∏ I ∈ p, w I : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ) :
      chernBicommutant C sX) = ∏ I ∈ p, (1 + s I) := fun p => by
    rw [Units.coe_prod]
    exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun I _ => hw I
  have hhalf : ∀ (p : Finset (Finset (Fin r))) (n : ℕ), TotalChowClass.homComponent n
      (((∏ I ∈ p, w I : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ) : chernBicommutant C sX) :
        TotalChowClass C sX) =
        ((subsetSumEsymm t p n : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) := fun p n => by
    rw [hcoeQ]
    exact homPart_coe_prod_one_add p s hsh n
  set e : TotalChowClass C sX :=
    (((Qe : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) with he
  set o : TotalChowClass C sX :=
    (((Qo : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) with ho
  set p : TotalChowClass C sX :=
    (((P : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ) : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX)
  have hΔ : ∀ n, TotalChowClass.homComponent n (e - o) =
      ((subsetSumEsymm t (evenCardSubsets r) n - subsetSumEsymm t (oddCardSubsets r) n :
        chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX) := fun n => by
    rw [map_sub, he, ho, hQe, hQo, hhalf, hhalf]
    exact (AddSubgroupClass.coe_sub _ _).symm
  have hΔlt : ∀ n < r, TotalChowClass.homComponent n (e - o) = 0 := fun n hn => by
    simp [hΔ, subsetSumEsymm_even_eq_odd t hn]
  have hmul : e - o = (p - 1) * o := by
    have h := congrArg (fun z : (chernBicommutant C sX)ˣ =>
      ((z : chernBicommutant C sX) : TotalChowClass C sX)) hregroup
    simp only [Units.val_mul, Subring.coe_mul] at h
    rw [he, ← h, sub_mul, one_mul]
  have ho0 : TotalChowClass.homComponent 0 o = 1 := by
    rw [ho, hQo, hhalf, subsetSumEsymm_zero, Subring.coe_one]
  have hW : ∀ n ≤ r,
      TotalChowClass.homComponent n (p - 1) = TotalChowClass.homComponent n (e - o) := by
    intro n
    induction n using Nat.strong_induction_on with
    | _ n ih =>
      intro hn
      rw [hmul, TotalChowClass.homComponent_mul_sum, Finset.sum_eq_single 0]
      · rw [Nat.sub_zero, ho0, mul_one]
      · intro j hj hj0
        have hjn : j ≤ n := Nat.lt_succ_iff.1 (Finset.mem_range.1 hj)
        rw [ih (n - j) (by omega) (by omega), hΔlt (n - j) (by omega), zero_mul]
      · exact fun h => (h (Finset.mem_range.2 n.succ_pos)).elim
  have hp : ∀ n, n ≠ 0 → n ≤ r →
      TotalChowClass.homComponent n p = TotalChowClass.homComponent n (e - o) := fun n hn0 hn => by
    rw [← hW n hn, map_sub, isHomogeneous_one.homPart_of_ne hn0, sub_zero]
  refine ⟨fun n hn0 hnr => by rw [hp n (by omega) hnr.le, hΔlt n hnr], ?_⟩
  rw [hp r hr le_rfl, hΔ, subsetSumEsymm_even_sub_odd t hr]
  push_cast
  rfl

end Alternating

/-! ### The Chern roots of the exterior powers -/

section Roots

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {T : Scheme.{u}} (sT : T ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sT]

/-- The two spellings of the tensor product of `𝒪_T`-modules, the one the exterior powers are
compared with and the one the twist formula is stated for, with the factors exchanged:
`ℒ ⊗ 𝒩 ≅ 𝒩 ⊗ ℒ`. -/
private def tensorSheafSwapIso (L N : T.Modules) :
    @Iso T.Modules _ (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor T.sheaf).obj L).obj N)
      (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor T.sheaf).obj N).obj L) :=
  (Scheme.Modules.ofSiteModules T).mapIso (Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorSheafCommIso _ L N)

/-- The total Chern class of `⋀⁰ ℰ ≅ 𝒪_T` is `1`. -/
theorem totalChern_exteriorPower_zero (E : T.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r] :
    haveI := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower E r 0
    totalChern C sT (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower E ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (r.choose 0) = 1 := by
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower E r 0
  have e0 : @Iso T.Modules _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower E ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ))
      (SheafOfModules.unit T.ringCatSheaf) :=
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.algebras _ E).exteriorPieceIso_zero
  have h1 : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower E ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ)) 1 := by
    simpa only [Nat.choose_zero_right] using
      Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower E r 0
  rw [totalChern_congr C sT (Iso.refl _) (Nat.choose_zero_right r)]
  exact totalChern_eq_one_of_iso_unit C sT _ e0

/-- The total Chern class of a module of rank one is `1 + c₁`. -/
theorem totalChern_eq_one_add_homPart_one (L : T.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} L 1] :
    totalChern C sT L 1 = 1 + TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sT L 1) := by
  refine ext_homPart fun n => ?_
  rw [map_add]
  rcases n with _ | _ | n
  · rw [homPart_zero_totalChern, isHomogeneous_one.homComponent_self,
      (TotalChowClass.isHomogeneous_homComponent 1 _).homPart_of_ne (by omega), add_zero]
  · rw [isHomogeneous_one.homPart_of_ne (by omega),
      (TotalChowClass.isHomogeneous_homComponent 1 _).homComponent_self]
    exact (zero_add _).symm
  · rw [homPart_totalChern_of_lt C sT L 1 (by omega), isHomogeneous_one.homPart_of_ne (by omega),
      (TotalChowClass.isHomogeneous_homComponent 1 _).homPart_of_ne (by omega), add_zero]

/-- **The total Chern classes of the exterior powers of an extension by a module of rank one.**
For a short exact sequence `0 ⟶ ℒ ⟶ ℰ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0` with `ℒ` of rank one and `𝒬` of rank `m`,

  `c(⋀^{k+1} ℰ) = T_{binom(m,k), c₁(ℒ)}(c(⋀^k 𝒬)) · c(⋀^{k+1} 𝒬)`,

by the Whitney sum formula on the sequence `0 ⟶ ℒ ⊗ ⋀^k 𝒬 ⟶ ⋀^{k+1} ℰ ⟶ ⋀^{k+1} 𝒬 ⟶ 0`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_shortExact_exteriorPower_of_rank_one`, and the
sequence itself for `k = 0`) and the twist formula of Stacks 02UD for `ℒ ⊗ ⋀^k 𝒬`. -/
theorem totalChern_exteriorPower_succ_of_shortExact {L E Q : T.Modules} (f : L ⟶ E) (g : E ⟶ Q)
    (w : f ≫ g = 0) (hS : (ShortComplex.mk f g w).ShortExact)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} L 1] (m : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} Q m]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E (m + 1)] (k : ℕ) :
    haveI := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower E (m + 1) (k + 1)
    haveI := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower Q m k
    haveI := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower Q m (k + 1)
    totalChern C sT (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower E ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) ((m + 1).choose (k + 1)) =
      twist (m.choose k : ℤ) (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sT L 1))
          (totalChern C sT (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower Q (k : ℤ)) (m.choose k)) *
        totalChern C sT (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower Q ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (m.choose (k + 1)) := by
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower E (m + 1) (k + 1)
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower Q m k
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower Q m (k + 1)
  have hLi : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible T.sheaf.obj T.ringCatSheaf.property L :=
    GenuineChern.isInvertible_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one L
  have hx : (TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sT L 1)).IsHomogeneous 1 :=
    TotalChowClass.isHomogeneous_homComponent 1 _
  rcases k with _ | k
  · -- `⋀¹ ℰ = ℰ`, `⋀⁰ 𝒬 = 𝒪`, `⋀¹ 𝒬 = 𝒬`, and the Whitney sum formula on the sequence itself
    have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E (1 + m) :=
      GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_shortExact _ hS 1 m ‹_› ‹_›
    have hW : totalChern C sT E (1 + m) = totalChern C sT L 1 * totalChern C sT Q m :=
      totalChern_eq_mul_of_shortExact C sT (ShortComplex.mk f g w) hS 1 m
    have eE : @Iso T.Modules _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower E ((0 + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) E :=
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.algebras _ E).exteriorPowerOneIso
    have eQ : @Iso T.Modules _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower Q ((0 + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) Q :=
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.algebras _ Q).exteriorPowerOneIso
    rw [totalChern_congr C sT eE ((Nat.choose_one_right (m + 1)).trans (Nat.add_comm m 1)), hW,
      totalChern_congr C sT eQ (Nat.choose_one_right m),
      show ((m.choose 0 : ℕ) : ℤ) = 1 by rw [Nat.choose_zero_right, Nat.cast_one],
      totalChern_exteriorPower_zero C sT Q m, twist_one_one hx,
      ← totalChern_eq_one_add_homPart_one C sT L]
  · -- the short exact sequence `0 ⟶ ℒ ⊗ ⋀^{k+1} 𝒬 ⟶ ⋀^{k+2} ℰ ⟶ ⋀^{k+2} 𝒬 ⟶ 0`
    obtain ⟨S, hSS, ⟨e₁⟩, ⟨e₂⟩, ⟨e₃⟩⟩ :=
      Scheme.Modules.exists_shortExact_exteriorPower_of_rank_one f g w hS m k
    have hT : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
        (R := T.ringCatSheaf) (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor T.sheaf).obj
          (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower Q ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))).obj L) (m.choose (k + 1)) :=
      GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_sheafTensor _ _ L
    let e₁' : @Iso T.Modules _ S.X₁ (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor T.sheaf).obj
        (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower Q ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ))).obj L) :=
      e₁ ≪≫ tensorSheafSwapIso L _
    have h₁ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₁
        (m.choose (k + 1)) :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.of_iso.{u, u, u} e₁'.symm hT
    have h₃ : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₃
        (m.choose (k + 1 + 1)) :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.of_iso.{u, u, u} e₃.symm
        (Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower Q m (k + 1 + 1))
    have hW := totalChern_eq_mul_of_shortExact C sT S hSS (m.choose (k + 1)) (m.choose (k + 1 + 1))
    have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} S.X₂
        (m.choose (k + 1) + m.choose (k + 1 + 1)) :=
      GenuineChern.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_shortExact _ hSS _ _ ‹_› ‹_›
    rw [totalChern_congr C sT e₂.symm (Nat.choose_succ_succ' m (k + 1)), hW,
      totalChern_congr C sT e₁' rfl, totalChern_congr C sT e₃ rfl,
      TotalChowClass.totalChern_sheafTensor C sT L _ (m.choose (k + 1)),
      firstChernTotal_eq_homComponent_totalChern]

/-- **The Chern roots of the exterior powers.** Let `ℳ` be an `𝒪_T`-module with a filtration of
length `r` whose successive quotients are invertible. Then there are classes `t_1, …, t_r` of
degree one in the bicommutant of the Chern classes — the first Chern classes of the successive
quotients — such that for every `n`

  `c(⋀ⁿ ℳ) = ∏_{I ⊆ {1, …, r}, #I = n} (1 + ∑_{i ∈ I} t_i)`.

This is the display of the proof of Stacks 0FEE. By induction on the filtration, read from its
bottom step (`Stacks.WeilCohomology.HasInvertibleFiltration.exists_shortExact_rankOne_sub`):
for `0 ⟶ ℒ ⟶ ℳ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0` with `ℒ` of rank one,
`Stacks.Chow.totalChern_exteriorPower_succ_of_shortExact` and the twist formula
`Stacks.Chow.twist_coe_prod_one_add` give the subsets containing the root `c₁(ℒ)` and
the subsets avoiding it (`Stacks.Chow.prod_powersetCard_succ_cons`). -/
theorem exists_chernRoots_exteriorPower {r : ℕ} {M : T.Modules}
    (h : Stacks.WeilCohomology.HasInvertibleFiltration T M r) :
    ∃ t : Fin r → chernBicommutant C sT, (∀ i, (t i : TotalChowClass C sT).IsHomogeneous 1) ∧
      ∀ n : ℕ, @totalChern C T sT _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower M (n : ℤ)) (r.choose n)
          (@Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower T M r n
            h.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank) =
        ((∏ I ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)).powersetCard n, (1 + ∑ i ∈ I, t i) :
          chernBicommutant C sT) : TotalChowClass C sT) := by
  induction r generalizing M with
  | zero =>
    have := h.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    refine ⟨Fin.elim0, fun i => i.elim0, fun n => ?_⟩
    rcases n with _ | n
    · rw [totalChern_exteriorPower_zero C sT M 0, Finset.powersetCard_zero, Finset.prod_singleton,
        Finset.sum_empty, add_zero, Subring.coe_one]
    · have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower M 0 (n + 1)
      rw [totalChern_eq_one_of_rank_eq_zero C sT _ _ (Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt (Nat.succ_pos n)),
        Finset.powersetCard_eq_empty.2 (by simp), Finset.prod_empty, Subring.coe_one]
  | succ r ih =>
    have := h.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    obtain ⟨L, Q, i, p, w, hS, hL1, hQ⟩ := h.exists_shortExact_rankOne_sub
    obtain ⟨s, hs, hQr⟩ := ih hQ
    have := hL1
    have := hQ.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    let x : chernBicommutant C sT := ⟨TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (totalChern C sT L 1),
      chernRing_le_chernBicommutant C sT
        (Subring.subset_closure (homPart_totalChern_mem_chernSet C sT L 1 1))⟩
    have hx : (x : TotalChowClass C sT).IsHomogeneous 1 :=
      TotalChowClass.isHomogeneous_homComponent 1 _
    refine ⟨Fin.cons x s, fun i => Fin.cases hx hs i, fun n => ?_⟩
    rcases n with _ | k
    · rw [totalChern_exteriorPower_zero C sT M (r + 1), Finset.powersetCard_zero,
        Finset.prod_singleton, Finset.sum_empty, add_zero, Subring.coe_one]
    · rw [totalChern_exteriorPower_succ_of_shortExact C sT i p w hS r k,
        prod_powersetCard_succ_cons (fun z => 1 + z) x s k, Subring.coe_mul, ← hQr (k + 1),
        hQr k, ← twist_coe_prod_one_add x hx _ _ (fun J => isHomogeneous_coe_sum J s hs),
        Finset.card_powersetCard, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin]

/-- The total Chern class of `ℳ` from the Chern roots of its exterior powers:
`c(ℳ) = c(⋀¹ ℳ) = ∏_i (1 + t_i)`. -/
theorem totalChern_eq_coe_prod_of_chernRoots {r : ℕ} (M : T.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} M r]
    (t : Fin r → chernBicommutant C sT)
    (h1 : @totalChern C T sT _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower M ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (r.choose 1)
        (Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower M r 1) =
      ((∏ I ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)).powersetCard 1, (1 + ∑ i ∈ I, t i) :
        chernBicommutant C sT) : TotalChowClass C sT)) :
    totalChern C sT M r = ((∏ i, (1 + t i) : chernBicommutant C sT) : TotalChowClass C sT) := by
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower M r 1
  have e : @Iso T.Modules _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower M ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) M :=
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.algebras _ M).exteriorPowerOneIso
  rw [← totalChern_congr C sT e (Nat.choose_one_right r), h1, Finset.powersetCard_one,
    Finset.prod_map]
  refine congrArg Subtype.val (Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_)
  simp

end Roots

/-! ### Stacks 0FEE -/

section AlternatingProduct

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- **The alternating product `∏_{n = 0}^{r} c(⋀ⁿ ℰ)^{(-1)ⁿ}`** of the total Chern classes of the
exterior powers of a finite locally free module `ℰ` of rank `r`, as a unit of the ring
`∏_p A^p(X)` of total Chow cohomology classes; `⋀ⁿ ℰ` has rank `binom(r, n)`. The ring of total
classes is not claimed to be commutative, so the product is taken in increasing order of `n`; its
factors commute with each other, Chern classes commuting by Stacks 02UA. -/
def altExteriorTotalChern (E : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r] :
    (TotalChowClass C sX)ˣ :=
  ((List.range (r + 1)).map fun n : ℕ =>
    @totalChernUnit C X sX _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower E (n : ℤ)) (r.choose n)
      (Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower E r n) ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ n)).prod

/-- **Restriction of the alternating product**: for `h : Y ⟶ X` the restriction of
`∏ c(⋀ⁿ ℰ)^{(-1)ⁿ}` is `∏ c(⋀ⁿ h^*ℰ)^{(-1)ⁿ}`, the exterior powers commuting with pullback
(Stacks 01CI, `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorPowerPullbackIso`). -/
theorem res_altExteriorTotalChern {Y : Scheme.{u}} {sY : Y ⟶ C.S} [LocallyOfFiniteType sY]
    (h : Y ⟶ X) [LocallyOfFiniteType h] (hs : h ≫ sX = sY) (E : X.Modules) (r : ℕ)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r] :
    letI := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank E r h
    res h hs (altExteriorTotalChern C sX E r : TotalChowClass C sX) =
      (altExteriorTotalChern C sY ((Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj E) r :
        TotalChowClass C sY) := by
  let := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank E r h
  have hcoe : ∀ z : (TotalChowClass C sX)ˣ, res h hs (z : TotalChowClass C sX) =
      ((Units.map (res h hs : TotalChowClass C sX →* TotalChowClass C sY) z :
        (TotalChowClass C sY)ˣ) : TotalChowClass C sY) := fun z => rfl
  rw [altExteriorTotalChern, altExteriorTotalChern, hcoe, map_list_prod, List.map_map]
  refine congrArg (fun z : (TotalChowClass C sY)ˣ => (z : TotalChowClass C sY))
    (congrArg List.prod (List.map_congr_left fun n _ => ?_))
  rw [Function.comp_apply, map_zpow]
  refine congrArg (· ^ ((-1 : ℤ) ^ n)) (Units.ext ?_)
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower E r n
  let := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower E (n : ℤ)) (r.choose n) h
  have := Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj E) r n
  rw [Units.coe_map, MonoidHom.coe_ofClass, val_totalChernUnit, val_totalChernUnit,
    TotalChowClass.res_totalChern]
  exact totalChern_congr C sY (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPowerPullbackIso h E (n : ℤ)) rfl

/-- **Stacks 0FEE.** Let `ℰ` be a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module of rank `r ≥ 1`. Then

  `∏_{n = 0}^{r} c(⋀ⁿ ℰ)^{(-1)ⁿ} = 1 - (r-1)! c_r(ℰ) + ⋯`,

that is, the alternating product of the total Chern classes of the exterior powers of `ℰ` has
vanishing parts in the degrees `1, …, r - 1` and the part `-(r-1)! c_r(ℰ)` in degree `r`; the part
in degree `0` is `1`, and the `⋯` of the source asserts nothing about the higher degrees. Here
`c_i(ℰ) = TotalChowClass.homComponent i (totalChern C sX ℰ r)` is the bivariant Chern class of
Stacks 0B7H in the ring `∏_p A^p(X)` of total Chow cohomology classes.

By the splitting principle (Stacks 02UL,
`Stacks.Chow.TotalChowClass.eq_of_res_eq_of_hasInvertibleFiltration`) it suffices to prove the
identities after restriction along every `h : T ⟶ X` along which `h^*ℰ` has a filtration with
invertible quotients. There `c(⋀ⁿ h^*ℰ) = ∏_{#I = n} (1 + ∑_{i ∈ I} x_i)` for the Chern roots
`x_i` (`Stacks.Chow.exists_chernRoots_exteriorPower`), and the alternating product of these is
computed by `Stacks.Chow.homPart_alternatingProd_of_roots`. -/
@[stacks 0FEE "the lemma as stated, for every X locally of finite type over S and every finite \
locally free E of rank r >= 1, with no further hypothesis. The alternating product is \
altExteriorTotalChern C sX E r, the ordered product of the units totalChernUnit of the exterior \
powers in the ring TotalChowClass C sX of total Chow cohomology classes; c_i(E) is \
TotalChowClass.homComponent i (totalChern C sX E r). The + ... of the source is read as \
asserting nothing above \
degree r, as its proof does"]
theorem homPart_altExteriorTotalChern (E : X.Modules) {r : ℕ}
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} E r] (hr : r ≠ 0) :
    (∀ n, 0 < n → n < r →
      TotalChowClass.homComponent n (altExteriorTotalChern C sX E r : TotalChowClass C sX) = 0) ∧
      TotalChowClass.homComponent r (altExteriorTotalChern C sX E r : TotalChowClass C sX) =
        -(Nat.factorial (r - 1) • TotalChowClass.homComponent r (totalChern C sX E r)) := by
  -- the identities on a test scheme along which `ℰ` is filtered
  have key : ∀ {T : Scheme.{u}} (sT : T ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sT] (h : T ⟶ X)
      [LocallyOfFiniteType h] (hs : h ≫ sX = sT),
      Stacks.WeilCohomology.HasInvertibleFiltration T ((Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj E) r →
      (∀ n, 0 < n → n < r →
        TotalChowClass.homComponent n
          (res h hs (altExteriorTotalChern C sX E r : TotalChowClass C sX)) = 0) ∧
        TotalChowClass.homComponent r
            (res h hs (altExteriorTotalChern C sX E r : TotalChowClass C sX)) =
          -(Nat.factorial (r - 1) •
            TotalChowClass.homComponent r (res h hs (totalChern C sX E r))) := by
    intro T sT _ h _ hs hfilt
    let := pullbackPreservesRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank E r h
    obtain ⟨t, ht, hroots⟩ := exists_chernRoots_exteriorPower C sT hfilt
    rw [res_altExteriorTotalChern, TotalChowClass.res_totalChern,
      totalChern_eq_coe_prod_of_chernRoots C sT _ t (hroots 1),
      homPart_coe_prod_one_add_univ t ht]
    exact homPart_alternatingProd_of_roots hr t ht (fun n =>
      @totalChernUnit C T sT _ (Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower ((Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj E)
        (n : ℤ)) (r.choose n) (Scheme.Modules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_exteriorPower _ r n))
      fun n _ => hroots n
  refine ⟨fun n hn0 hnr => ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine TotalChowClass.eq_of_res_eq_of_hasInvertibleFiltration (I := Unit) (fun _ => E)
      (fun _ => r) (fun _ => ‹_›) fun {T} sT _ h _ hs hfilt => ?_
    rw [TotalChowClass.res_homComponent, map_zero]
    exact (key sT h hs (hfilt ())).1 n hn0 hnr
  · refine TotalChowClass.eq_of_res_eq_of_hasInvertibleFiltration (I := Unit) (fun _ => E)
      (fun _ => r) (fun _ => ‹_›) fun {T} sT _ h _ hs hfilt => ?_
    rw [TotalChowClass.res_homComponent, map_neg, map_nsmul, TotalChowClass.res_homComponent]
    exact (key sT h hs (hfilt ())).2

end AlternatingProduct

